  "rationale": "This batch directly targets previously uncovered contract clauses and counterexamples: (1) isolated key namespace across different tenants sharing identical key names; (2) idempotency during active reservations without repeated stock reduction; (3) payload conflict specifically when quantity differs for an existing key; (4) idempotent release ensuring stock is restored exactly once; (5) strict case sensitivity without case folding on tenant and key identifiers; (6) requirement to validate all fields first even when replaying an already-reserved key with invalid parameters; (7) validation handling for malformed/missing fields on release, stock, and unknown ops; and (8) upper boundary quantity allocation (qty=10) draining inventory to 0, rejecting subsequent reserves, and recovering via release.",
  "origin": "live Google DeepMind / Gemini; fresh context, implementation withheld"
